Upon closer inspection of the relevant section in [the methodological document](./emissions_db_construction.qmd#tbl-edgar-domains) and the [processing step](./emdb_processing.html#bind-final-datasets) in the code we can see that this data comes directly from the EDGAR dataset. More specifically we can see that we only replaced elements `1.A.*` with our own estimates from coefficients, while the offending element belongs to `1.B.*`.


::: {.cell}

```{#lst-edgar-filter .r .cell-code  lst-cap="Filter in processing code only replaces 1.A. (! negates match)"}
gwp_total_emissions3 <- gwp_total_emissions4 |>
  filter(
    !startsWith(`IPCC Code`, "1.A."),
  )
```
:::


Knowing that the estimate is correct, the fault lies in our process step where we associate each emission from Edgar to an ISIC sector. Mozambique is a producer of coal and it is evident that that sector which is producing the solid fuels fugitive emissions and not the distributing service sector. We mistakenly associated **1.B.1 Solid Fuels** with **4661 Wholesale of solid, liquid and gaseous fuels and related products**, which is a service, while the correct association should be with Division **"05 Mining of coal and lignite"**. Since there is no driver to identify whether it is coal (ISIC 0501) or lignite(ISIC 0502), we will compromise and keep it at the division level, only identifying it as 0500 for correct ordering. This means we have updated the `GWP ISIC` spreadsheet tab in `/data/classifications/equivalence.xlsx` to reflect this change.
